# Environment variables
# .env.* is a blanket rule on purpose: it covers .env.local, .env.production and
# ad-hoc copies like .env.bak.<date>, any of which holds live credentials that a
# `git add -A` would otherwise stage. The template is the one exception.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

